        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(deepgram): reject malformed and non-http(s) realtime base URL overrides",
        "body": "<details>\n<summary>Additional instructions</summary>\n\n**MUST:** Keep **Allow edits from maintainers** enabled for this PR so maintainers\ncan help update the branch when needed.\n\n</details>\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where a malformed or non-HTTP(S) Deepgram `baseUrl` in provider config crashes\nrealtime transcription session setup with an uncaught `TypeError: Invalid URL`, or is silently\naccepted for a scheme that downstream fetch/WebSocket paths cannot use.\n\n`normalizeDeepgramRealtimeBaseUrl` in `extensions/deepgram/realtime-transcription-provider.ts`\nonly trimmed the value — it never confirmed the result was a parseable HTTP(S) URL. Its consumer\n`toDeepgramRealtimeWsUrl` does `new URL(normalizeDeepgramRealtimeBaseUrl(config.baseUrl))` and then\nrewrites the protocol to `ws:`/`wss:`.\n\n**Concrete example:** with `baseUrl: \"not a url\"`, `normalizeDeepgramRealtimeBaseUrl` on current\n`main` returns `\"not a url\"` and the downstream `new URL(\"not a url\")` throws an opaque\n`TypeError: Invalid URL`. A value like `ftp://host` parses but is not a usable Deepgram endpoint,\nyet is accepted and rewritten into a `ws:`/`wss:` URL.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nValidate the base URL at the normalizer boundary and **fail actionably**: only an absent/blank value\n(or unset `DEEPGRAM_BASE_URL`) falls back to the default endpoint; an explicit value that is\nunparseable, or whose scheme is not `http:`/`https:`, throws a clear `Invalid Deepgram baseUrl` error.\nThis mirrors the merged `fix(microsoft-foundry): reject malformed endpoints` (#104796) precedent and\nthe sibling ElevenLabs fix (#105163). An operator's explicit endpoint is their intent, so it is never\nsilently swapped for the default. The validation errors are redacted — they never echo the raw\nconfigured URL, so embedded userinfo or credential-bearing query params are not disclosed to\nlogs/diagnostics.\n\n## User Impact\n\n**Before:** a mistyped Deepgram `baseUrl` surfaces an opaque `TypeError: Invalid URL` at session setup,\nand a non-HTTP(S) endpoint is accepted and produces unusable WebSocket URLs.\n\n**After:** an explicit malformed or non-HTTP(S) `baseUrl` fails fast with an actionable, secret-safe\nerror; absent/blank config still defaults; valid custom `http(s)` endpoints are unchanged.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `extensions/deepgram/realtime-transcription-provider.ts` — `normalizeDeepgramRealtimeBaseUrl` rejects explicit malformed / non-HTTP(S) values (throws) and only defaults absent/blank input; error messages surface only \"value is not a valid URL\" or the offending `protocol`, never the raw URL. Exposed via the existing `testing` object for coverage.\n- Regression test: `extensions/deepgram/realtime-transcription-provider.test.ts` — asserts absent/blank → default, valid → normalized, explicit malformed → throws, `ftp:` → throws `unsupported scheme`, and a `baseUrl` with userinfo + `api_key` query is rejected without its secret/token appearing in the error. These fail on the pre-fix trim-only version.\n- Function probe against the real production helper (via `testing`):\n\n```\n$ node --import tsx -e \"import('./extensions/deepgram/realtime-transcription-provider.ts').then(m => …)\"\nundefined -> \"https://api.deepgram.com/v1\"\n\"https://custom.example.com\" -> \"https://custom.example.com\"\n\"not a url\" -> THROWS: Invalid Deepgram baseUrl: value is not a valid URL\n\"ftp://user:sup3r-secret@files.example.com?api_key=leak-me\" -> THROWS: Invalid Deepgram baseUrl: unsupported scheme \"ftp:\" (expected http or https)\n```\n\n(The credential-bearing input is rejected with no `sup3r-secret` / `leak-me` / `api_key` in the message.)\n",
        "branch": "fix/deepgram-baseurl-validate",
        "head_sha": "5f9467e299c647b2cd95b28045d76ec6d5e48f96",
